    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Sample paths of standard Brownian motion spread like \sqrt{t}: at time t, W(t) \sim \mathcal N(0, t), so about 95% of paths lie within \pm 2\sqrt t. The quadratic variation \sum (\Delta W)^2 equals t, the signature of a path that is continuous but nowhere differentiable.">

